  "notes": "Cash basis county, governmental activities only. Governmental funds statement p4 Total Governmental Funds column used. Printed ending 2,050,934 is 1 more than roll-forward (rounding in report). Local receipts line has no printed breakdown; categorized by the dominant source per the p2 Statement of Activities (see RECHECK below), with review. Detail: budget schedules for General, Road and Bridge, Highway Bridge Buyback, Inheritance Tax and Nonmajor funds recorded; p11 combining schedule of nonmajor funds (balances, receipts, disbursements by fund, no categories) not recorded in detail to avoid double counting with the Nonmajor budget schedule. Road and Bridge federal receipts had budget 189,000 and no actual (not recorded). Buyback and Inheritance Tax funds print no total lines. Operating expenses mapped to professional/contract services as guess. Statements of Activities p2 shows property tax 1,282,171, state receipts 164,535, other receipts 113,303 for governmental activities (different presentation, not used for splits). Read pages 1-11 of 11. RECHECK: top-level Local 1,538,091 split by p4 fund column into Inheritance Tax Fund 33,755 (inheritance tax) and the rest 1,504,336 (property tax, review); General and Road and Bridge detail Local lines recategorised to property tax (dominant per p2 bounds) to match. AUDIT3: the Nonmajor column Local 4,200 (p4) was moved out of the property-tax line into its own receipt (category other, review), matching the Nonmajor budget schedule detail line; p11 shows it is Preservation and Modernization, Opioid Recovery, Law Enforcement and Noxious Weed fund receipts, not property tax."
